  "question": {
    "text": "Let the vertices $Q$ and $R$ of the triangle $P Q R$ lie on the line $\\frac{x+3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3}, Q R=5$ and the coordinates of the point $P$ be $(0,2,3)$. If the area of the triangle $P Q R$ is $\\frac{m}{n}$ then :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5siKg",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{m}-5 \\sqrt{21} \\mathrm{n}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lW74k",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~m}-5 \\sqrt{21} \\mathrm{n}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tDZH9",
      "text": "$5 \\mathrm{~m}-2 \\sqrt{21} \\mathrm{n}=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d3PsW",
      "text": "$5 m-21 \\sqrt{2} n=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/n82HzxhTcZnoqId4AkS1dZNJzt0P74BrZMZ11auEfM8.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\mathrm{M}(5 \\lambda-3,2 \\lambda+1,3 \\lambda-4)$<br/>Drs of PM $\\Rightarrow 5 \\lambda-3,2 \\lambda-1,3 \\lambda-7$<br/>Drs of line $L \\Rightarrow 5,2,3$<br/>$\\mathrm{PM} \\perp \\mathrm{L}$<br/>$\\Rightarrow(5 \\lambda-3) 5+(2 \\lambda-1) 2+(3 \\lambda-7) 3=0$<br/>$\\Rightarrow \\lambda=1$<br/>$\\therefore \\mathrm{M}(2,3,-1)$<br/>$P M=\\sqrt{4+1+16}=\\sqrt{21}$<br/>Area $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times \\sqrt{21}=\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{n}}$<br/>$2 \\mathrm{~m}-5 \\sqrt{21} \\mathrm{n}=0$",
    "image": null
  },
